<title>USA: Wissahickon, Pa., schools yield 5.10 pct in 2008.</title>
<headline>Wissahickon, Pa., schools yield 5.10 pct in 2008.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dolphin &amp; Bradbury said Monday it priced $18.8 million Wissahickon School District, Pa., general obligation bonds, series 1996, at a top yield of 5.10 percent in 2008.</p>
<p>The pricing follows:</p>
<p>WISSAHICKON SCHOOL DISTRICT</p>
<p>RE: $18,810,000</p>
<p>MONGOMERY COUNTY, PA., GO SERIES 1996</p>
<p>FIRST INTEREST PAYMENT: 5/15/1997</p>
<p>MOODY'S: AA</p>
<p>DATED 12/15/1996</p>
<p>DUE 11/15</p>
<p>CALL: 11/15/2002</p>
<p>DELIVERY: EXPECTED 12/27/1996</p>
<p>    11/15	   Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(million)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1997	    $1.120	  4.50	  3.60</p>
<p>    1998	    $1.170	  3.90	  3.90</p>
<p>    1999	    $1.220	  4.15	  4.15</p>
<p>    2000	    $1.275	  4.20	  4.20</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.755	  4.30	  4.30</p>
<p>    2002	    $0.785	  4.45	  4.45</p>
<p>    2003	    $0.820	  4.60	  4.60</p>
<p>    2004	    $0.855	  4.65	  4.70</p>
<p>    2005	    $1.515	  4.75	  4.80</p>
<p>    2006	    $4.325	  4.85	  4.90</p>
<p>    2007	    $4.545	  5.00	  5.00</p>
<p>    2008	    $0.425	  5.00	  5.10</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
